      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic cast HfNbTaTiZr has a yield strength of 163–530 MPa at 1000 °C.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic cast HfNbTaTiZr has inadequate oxygen resistance.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 3–5 at.% Al to equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr will cause an Al2O3 surface scale to form during high-temperature exposure in air.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::rubric_card::000::c40db9eaa7"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al2O3 formed on the Al-modified alloy will be thin, continuous, and adherent.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperature, aluminum will preferentially oxidize relative to the constituent elements of HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting Al2O3 layer will be stable and slow-growing.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al2O3 layer will act as a barrier to oxygen ingress.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed oxide barrier will minimize internal oxidation and pesting.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 3–5 at.% Al will not adversely affect solid-solution strengthening or ductility in the HfNbTaTiZr matrix.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At approximately 800 °C in air for up to 5 hours, the Al-modified alloy will have a lower oxidation rate than untreated equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The lower oxidation rate will be manifested by lower mass gain and less oxide penetration.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified alloy will retain room-temperature tensile ductility comparable to that of untreated equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified alloy will retain high-temperature yield strength comparable to untreated equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr at 1000 °C and strain rates of 10^-4–10^-2 s^-1.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Untreated equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr undergoes rapid oxidation or pesting in air at approximately 800 °C.",
